      "retrieved": "2026-10-17",
      "revision": 1313766217,
      "text": "Agave bovicornuta Gentry, is a plant in the genus Agave, native to mountainous regions in the Mexican states of Chihuahua, Sonora and Sinaloa. The common name Cowhorn Agave and the specific epithet refer to the prominent red spines along the edges of the leaves. Other common names include \"lechguilla verde\""
